menu "AirTrack board"

choice AIRTRACK_BOARD
    prompt "Target board"
    default AIRTRACK_BOARD_LCD_1_47
    help
        AirTrack is board-specific: the pin map, panel geometry, backlight
        path, and available peripherals all differ between supported boards.
        Select the board this image is built for.  Installing an image built
        for the wrong board leaves the display dark; the OTA manifest carries
        a board identifier so the device refuses a mismatched update.

    config AIRTRACK_BOARD_LCD_1_47
        bool "Waveshare ESP32-C6-LCD-1.47"
        help
            172 x 320 ST7789 on SPI2, 34-pixel X RAM offset, backlight on
            GPIO22 (LEDC), WS2812B status LED on GPIO8, microSD on GPIO4,
            8 MB flash.  This is the original AirTrack target.

    config AIRTRACK_BOARD_TOUCH_LCD_2_8
        bool "Waveshare ESP32-C6-Touch-LCD-2.8"
        help
            240 x 320 ST7789 on SPI2 with no RAM offset.  Panel reset and
            backlight PWM are reached through the on-board CH32V003 I/O
            expander at I2C address 0x24 rather than through ESP32 GPIO.
            There is no WS2812 status LED.  microSD on GPIO23, 16 MB flash.
            A PCF85063A RTC and an SHTC3 temperature/humidity sensor share
            the expander's I2C bus and are used when present.  The CST3530
            touch panel is not used by AirTrack.

endchoice

endmenu
